{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"bared-nickel-insect","creation_channel":"cli","description":"Dependabot PR #124 bumps mcp 1.29.0 -> 2.0.0, but mcp 2.0 removes the mcp.server.fastmcp module (verified: ModuleNotFoundError) that rebar's MCP server imports (src/rebar/mcp_server.py:512,570,590; src/rebar/_mcp_auth.py:38; src/rebar/_mcp_models.py:287; scripts/gen_mcp_reference.py:72). Migrating is structural work: port to the mcp 2.0 server API (fastmcp equivalents / mcp-types), update the mcp>=1.28.1,<2 constraint in pyproject.toml (mcp + dev extras), .github/workflows/_optionality.yml:105, and amend ADR 0050:28 (keep the GHSA-9h52-p55h-vw2f floor rationale). Validate with tests/interfaces/facades/test_mcp*.py and the workflow-schema test. Deferred out of ticket 1dfd per its path-2 decision rule.","id":"732b-51df-acf2-477b","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"task","title":"Migrate MCP server to mcp 2.0 (fastmcp removal)"},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1785713940797246001,"uuid":"e726eee3-da52-464a-82e7-a0a1b84cd0ba"}